--TEST--
`static` on a `constructor` is `E0106` at the modifier, and a `static` method with another name that returns `new self(...)` compiles
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Point {
    public int $x = 0;

    public function constructor(int $x) {
        $this->x = $x;
    }

    public static function origin(): Point {
        return new self(0);
    }
}

class Counter {
    public int $start = 0;

    public static function constructor(int $n) {}
}

echo Point::origin()->x, "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0106]: `static` is not allowed on a constructor
%A
17 |     public static function constructor(int $n) {}
   |            ^^^^^^ delete this modifier
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
